## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP over multiple segments with a budget and in/out state tracking to allow adjacency.

## Key Concepts
- DP with segment count and in/out state
- Transitions for starting, extending, and ending a segment
- Handling adjacency and at-most-k constraint

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(a, k){
  const n = a.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  // dp[i][t][s] -> max sum using first i elements
  let dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array.from({length: k+1}, ()=> [NEG, NEG]));
  dp[0][0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    for(let t=0;t<=k;t++){
      for(let s=0;s<2;s++){
        const cur = dp[i][t][s];
        if(cur===NEG) continue;
        if(s===0){
          // skip a[i]
          dp[i+1][t][0] = Math.max(dp[i+1][t][0], cur);
          // start new
          if(t<k) dp[i+1][t+1][1] = Math.max(dp[i+1][t+1][1], cur + a[i]);
        } else {
          // extend
          dp[i+1][t][1] = Math.max(dp[i+1][t][1], cur + a[i]);
          // end
          dp[i+1][t][0] = Math.max(dp[i+1][t][0], cur);
        }
      }
    }
  }
  let ans = 0;
  for(let t=0;t<=k;t++) ans = Math.max(ans, dp[n][t][0], dp[n][t][1]);
  return ans;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a partition DP where segment values depend on a non-trivial per-substring metric (distinct counts). It extends simple sum-based DP to a more nuanced local score.

## Key Concepts
- DP over i and t to build up k segments
- Precompute distinctCount(l,r) for all substrings
- Backpointers to recover exact endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxDistinctSegments(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const cnt = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let L = 0; L < n; L++) {
    const freq = new Array(26).fill(0);
    let d = 0;
    for (let R = L; R < n; R++) {
      const idx = s.charCodeAt(R) - 97;
      if (freq[idx]++ === 0) d++;
      cnt[L][R] = d;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= Math.min(i, k); t++) {
      for (let p = t-1; p <= i-1; p++) {
        const val = dp[p][t-1] + cnt[p][i-1];
        if (val > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = val; par[i][t] = p; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct endpoints from par
}
```

